sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-competency-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In the 1D artificial embryogeny model, when competency is set by an evolvable gene (range 1–500, initialized at 1–15), the best individual's competency rose rapidly and plateaued around 470, higher than the roughly 364 needed for maximum fitness, a level the authors attribute to random drift among equally fit values.";
    dc:type "simulation-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Evolvable competency rises rapidly and plateaus at a high level";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Shreesha L, Levin M, “Cellular Competency during Development Alters Evolutionary Dynamics in an Artificial Embryogeny Model”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2023), doi:10.3390/e25010131; section “3. Results › 3.4. Evolution Results in a High, Constant Level of Competency”. Scope: In silico 1D artificial embryos with an evolvable competency gene over 1000 generations"
}
